From 39875517c04b99103f501df9ec522b60b07b137a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: buzzcast <you@example.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:53:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 2.1: close two ways the honesty gate could be bypassed

Found while auditing whether the gate was too permissive on thin evidence.

1. "Follow the bot" ignored the gate entirely (serious)
   place_bet() applied the tier's stake multiplier only in the provisional
   case, so following the bot on a `pass` tier placed a full Kelly stake
   while the bot was telling you to sit the turn out. The gate itself was
   correct; the click a user actually makes went around it. The original
   suite could not see this because every test gates on pred["committed"]
   before calling place_bet - verified by reintroducing the bug, which left
   32/34 tests green. Two new tests exercise the click directly.
   Concretely: 74-82% peak drawdowns on simulated fair games, vs 0-24% now.

2. Provisional stakes were licensed by uncorrected evidence
   A signal clearing only the ordinary 5% bar could buy a hedged position.
   That bar is evaluated every turn and against every colour, so it fires
   constantly on a fair game and the hedges compound into ruinous variance.
   A stake now requires one line of evidence that survives the Bonferroni
   correction (or a corrected-frequency edge with a non-negative paper
   trade). Marginal evidence buys nothing.
   This also sends the old 70-result archive to `pass` instead of a hedged
   bet: its 3.4% lean fails the corrected bar and its compression edge is
   negative, i.e. two weak signals pointing opposite ways.

Kept deliberately: a real edge is still found everywhere it exists
(biased 1k->48k, markov_strong 1k->72k, thin markov 1k->150k over 2000
turns), and a negative compression edge does NOT by itself block a stake -
a badly calibrated model can still have a profitable favourite, so requiring
both lines of evidence would block real bets.

Also:
- simulate: `bot` now mirrors the button exactly (tier scale included);
  added `bot_strict` for commitments only. The lab and live play can no
  longer drift apart.
- UI: the Simulation-lab dropdowns were never populated (blank values on
  submit); now filled from labelled source/policy lists including bot_strict.
- README: documents the corrected-evidence rule and both bugs.

34 tests, in ~5s.
